  },
  {
    "id": "method-daily-granite-cleaner",
    "name": "Method Daily Granite Cleaner",
    "category": "Daily Surface Cleaner, Plant-Based",
    "badge": "Best Low-Fragrance Option",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Positioned by the manufacturer as a streak-free daily cleaner for stone countertops",
      "Plant-derived cleaning agents suit households that prefer gentler ingredient lists",
      "Pump-spray bottle is easy to keep beside the sink and use one-handed",
      "Pairs well with a microfibre cloth for matte finishes where streaks show"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Not a degreaser, so heavy cooking residue needs a second pass",
      "The scented varieties will not suit everyone"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A good second choice for the daily wipe if you want a gentler formula. Use it where light, frequent cleaning is the pattern.",
    "description": "The point of a daily stone cleaner is that you will actually use it. A spray that smells pleasant, works on a quick wipe and does not feel like a chore tends to get used every evening, and a surface wiped every evening is rarely a surface with a stain problem. Method Daily Granite Cleaner is aimed at exactly that habit. The manufacturer markets it as a streak-free cleaner for granite, quartz and similar stone, which in practice means it is safe to treat as a general stone-surface spray. Sintered stone owners often prefer a pH-neutral or mild product because they have been told, correctly, that the surface does not need aggressive chemistry. The best technique is to spray lightly, wipe in one direction with a damp microfibre cloth, then buff dry. That final buff does more for a streak-free result than the choice of spray does."
  },
  {
    "id": "weiman-granite-stone-cleaner-polish",
    "name": "Weiman Granite & Stone Cleaner and Polish",
    "category": "Cleaner and Polish, Gloss Finishes",
    "badge": "Best for Polished Finishes",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "pros": [
      "Cleans and adds shine in one step on polished or silk-gloss surfaces",
