    "description": "Every kitchen eventually gets a film. It is a thin layer of cooking oil, soap residue and mineral deposits that makes a surface look flat even though nothing is stained. Daily sprays are not built to cut that, and abrasive scrubbing is the wrong response on a surface people pay a premium to keep looking new. StoneTech is a stone-care brand that is widely used by professionals, and its Revitalizer line is sold as a stone cleaner and protector. For sintered stone, the useful part is the cleaning action. The surface is non-porous, so a protecting step is not what it needs. Use it sparingly, rinse well, and finish with a dry microfibre cloth. If the manufacturer of your slab lists approved cleaners, check that list first, because it takes precedence over any retail label."
