    "bottomLine": "A spot-treatment tool, not a daily cleaner. Use it rarely and gently, and check your slab manufacturer first.",
    "description": "Sintered stone resists staining better than most countertop materials, but \"resists\" is not \"immune\". Dark metallic marks from pans, rust rings from cans and mineral deposits around a tap can sit on the surface and need something stronger than a spray. Bar Keepers Friend Soft Cleanser is a long-standing option for that, and its active ingredient is oxalic acid. The honest caveat is finish. A mild abrasive acting on a polished or silk surface can dull it, and the damage is rarely reversible. On textured or matte surfaces it is more forgiving. Treat it as the last step before asking your fabricator. Apply a small amount, work gently with a soft cloth, rinse thoroughly and dry. If the mark does not move after two gentle attempts, stop and read your slab manufacturer care guide rather than escalating the scrubbing."
